<title>LEBANON: MEA airline stewards suspend one-day strike.</title>
<headline>MEA airline stewards suspend one-day strike.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-02-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stewards of Lebanon's national carrier Middle East Airlines suspended a 24-hour strike planned for Sunday after the company pledged to meet their pay demands, MEA stewards union sources said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The sources said an understanding was reached with the company late on Saturday evening. Under the deal, MEA will propose a new pay scale for stewards within three weeks.</p>
<p>The union grouping the airliner's 355 stewards had planned to go on strike immediately after midnight Saturday.</p>
<p>Activity was normal at Beirut airport on Sunday with 12 scheduled MEA flights leaving the country and 13 flights coming in.</p>
</text>
